    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d291">

                <pb facs="0382" n="370" sameAs="frus:frus1944v03/pg370"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EW/8–2644: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé to the Greek Government in Exile</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Shantz</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-08-26T13:00:00+03:00">August 26, 1944—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 26—8:31 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Greek 263. Telegram from Eden to Lord Moyne dated August 25 asks that Moyne
                    present armistice terms to Bulgarian delegate now at Istanbul who is being sent
                    to Cairo for this purpose. This disagrees with Department’s 71, August
                        25.<anchor n="26" xml:id="d291-f1"/> Because of better communication with
                    Bulgaria, Steel<anchor n="27" xml:id="d291-f2"/> strongly favors negotiation at
                    Ankara and is advising London to this effect.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Murphy as 21, to Ankara and to London as 8.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shantz</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
